# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings, even on Windows.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and ships scripts that run on macOS and Linux. A .sh file checked
# out with CRLF fails in ways that read as logic bugs rather than encoding ones — bash takes the
# trailing \r as part of the last token on the line, so you get "unbound variable" or "command not
# found" naming something that is plainly right there in the file.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else consumed by a POSIX tool where a stray \r changes behaviour.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
